<title>BELGIUM: W. Europe car registrations down in Jan - ACEA.</title>
<headline>W. Europe car registrations down in Jan - ACEA.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>New passenger car registrations in Western Europe fell 2.9 percent in January to 1,130,000 units compared with the same month last year, the European Automobile Manufacturers Association (ACEA) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Among the different countries included in the monthly survey, car registrations plunged 33.7 percent in France and 26.3 percent in Switzerland.</p>
<p>But they increased by 28.4 percent in Sweden, 22.1 percent in Spain and by 20.7 percent in Ireland.</p>
<p>-- Fredrik Dahl + 32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
